From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:54:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: apple: atc: support the T8132 CIO mode

Run USB4 and Thunderbolt on T8132 PHYs that have their CIO calibration.
After the power-up handshake the PHY gets that calibration, both lanes go
to CIO and the crossbar follows the plug orientation; the PHY then brings
up its PLLs and lanes itself, driven by the host router. Leaving CIO takes
the common block down and clamps the transmitters before the resets, as
the end of the mode4 stop already does.

USB2 stays up beside CIO, and the PHY keeps its power domain for as long
as the mode is set, which the host router depends on.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
[eryk: tools/asahi/atc-usb3-tests.py and the apple-dcp selftests compile
 the mux and PIPE functions changed here, and no longer built: give them
 atcphy_mode_is_cio(), atcphy_pipe_state_for() and cio_tunables, and move
 two atc-usb3 mutation sites to the new helper. Both pass again: 36 cases
 and 49/49 mutants, and 85/85 apple-dcp units]
Signed-off-by: Eryk Wieliczko <eryk@wieliczko.ninja>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(backported from commit 1f5936fa82e30bb6ba69160bc2c46547207be2f0)
[j604: Driver change as upstream. The apple-dcp host harness hunks
 (common.py, dwc3/mocks.c, lifecycle.py, phy.py, quiesce.py) are taken;
